    <body data-sd-ui-layer-boundary="true"><div id="MathJax_Message" style="display: none;"></div>
      <script type="text/javascript">
        window.__PRELOADED_STATE__ = {"abstracts":{"content":[{"$$":[{"$":{"id":"d1e2006"},"#name":"section-title","_":"Abstract"},{"$$":[{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2009"},"#name":"simple-para","$$":[{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"__text__","_":"The most crucial design constraint on the "},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"Internet of Things","$":{"href":"/topics/engineering/internet-of-things","term":"Internet of Things"}},{"#name":"__text__","_":" (IoT) enabled "}]},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"wireless sensor networks","$":{"href":"/topics/engineering/wireless-sensor-network","term":"wireless sensor networks"}},{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"__text__","_":" (WSNs) is "},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"energy dissipation","$":{"href":"/topics/engineering/energy-dissipation","term":"energy dissipation"}},{"#name":"__text__","_":". The inefficient data collection by the resource constraint sensors becomes a major roadblock in energy preservation to achieve network longevity. The energy of nodes has to be utilized in an efficient manner which helps in increasing the longevity of WSNs. Clustering is a technique that can utilize the energy of the sensors efficiently by maintaining load balancing among the sensors for increasing the lifetime and scalability of the networks. In this paper, the energy consumption of the network is improved by considering the "}]},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"Genetic Algorithm","$":{"href":"/topics/engineering/genetic-algorithm","term":"Genetic Algorithm"}},{"#name":"text","$$":[{"#name":"__text__","_":" evolutionary computing technique. The proposed OptiGACHS protocol describes the improved cluster head (CH) "},{"#name":"topic-link","_":"selection procedure","$":{"href":"/topics/engineering/selection-procedure","term":"selection procedure"}},{"#name":"__text__","_":" by incorporating criteria of distance, density, energy, and heterogeneous node‚Äôs capability for developing fitness function. The OptiGACHS protocol operates with single, multiple static, and multiple movable sinks to have an impartial comparative examination. Multiple movable sinks are proposed to shorten transmission distance between the sink and CH and also pact with the hot-spot problem. A deployment strategy for nodes is also discussed for energy and distance optimization during network operation. It is observed from simulations that the proposed OptiGACHS protocol outperforms existing protocols."}]}]}]}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2008"},"#name":"abstract-sec"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2005","class":"author"},"#name":"abstract"},{"$$":[{"$":{"id":"d1e2014"},"#name":"section-title","_":"Highlights"},{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$$":[{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"‚Ä¢"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2023"},"#name":"para","_":"An Optimize GA for Cluster Head Selection protocol is proposed for IoT enabled WSN."}],"$":{"id":"d1e2020"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"‚Ä¢"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2028"},"#name":"para","_":"To alleviate hot-spot problem, multiple movable sinks in network are incorporated."}],"$":{"id":"d1e2025"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"‚Ä¢"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2033"},"#name":"para","_":"A new deployment strategy is considered for optimization of network energy."}],"$":{"id":"d1e2030"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"‚Ä¢"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2038"},"#name":"para","_":"Performance evaluation of OptiGACHS variants is done against the GAOC and MS-GAOC."}],"$":{"id":"d1e2035"},"#name":"list-item"},{"$$":[{"#name":"label","_":"‚Ä¢"},{"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2043"},"#name":"para","_":"OptiGACHS variants are developed for unattended hostile applications."}],"$":{"id":"d1e2040"},"#name":"list-item"}],"$":{"id":"d1e2019"},"#name":"list"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2017"},"#name":"simple-para"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2016"},"#name":"abstract-sec"}],"$":{"view":"all","id":"d1e2013","class":"author-highlights"},"#name":"abstract"}],"floats":[],"f